course: dictionary
lesson: 15213
title: Sensitivity: caring and noticing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sensitivity is a noun, so it names something you can have. It comes from sensitive, which means easily affected by feelings or things around you. «Mia noticed that Sam was quiet at lunch, so she sat beside him and did not ask why.» Mia showed sensitivity: she noticed how Sam felt and was careful with him.
explain: Sensitivity can also mean how easily something reacts or gets hurt. «Ben has tooth sensitivity, so cold ice cream makes his teeth ache.» Here the word describes a body part that reacts strongly to cold.
explain: In science, sensitivity means how well a tool can notice very small changes. «The microphone has high sensitivity, so it picks up a whisper across the room.» The more sensitive the tool, the smaller the change it can notice.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If the sentence is about feelings, sensitivity means care for others. If it is about a tool, it means how well the tool notices tiny things. The context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Sensitivity is a noun, and its plural is sensitivities.
fact: «Sensitivity» can mean being kind and careful about other people's feelings.
fact: «Sensitivity» can mean how easily something reacts or is hurt, such as «sensitivity to light».
fact: A «sensitivity» can be a mild allergy or bad reaction to something, such as «gluten sensitivity».
fact: The sensitivity of a topic is how likely it is to upset people.
exercise: In «Mia showed great sensitivity when Sam was sad», what does sensitivity mean? | *Being kind and careful about other people's feelings | Being very tired | Being quick at running | Being good at sums
exercise: Ben has tooth sensitivity. What does this mean? | His teeth are very white | He brushes his teeth twice a day | *His teeth react and hurt easily, especially to cold | He has lost a tooth
exercise: A microphone with high sensitivity does what? | *Notices very small sounds and changes | Makes every sound stop | Turns itself off | Plays music very loudly
test: Which sentence uses sensitivity to mean kindness? | *«Lily showed sensitivity by waiting quietly while her friend cried.» | «The sensitivity of the mouse was turned up, so the cursor jumped.» | «Ravi has a sensitivity to peanuts.» | «The thermometer has a high sensitivity.»
test: What does the sensitivity of a topic mean? | *How likely it is to upset people | How long a topic lasts | How many people like it | How loud it is
exam: In «The sensitive microphone picked up a tiny tap», what does sensitive show about the microphone? | How angry a person is | How fast a car can drive | How tall a tree grows | *How well a tool notices very small changes
